From dbb48e6e0647eea22804953ac3ac7bd80d532765 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 16:42:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/10] feat(control-plane): degrade Ready services whose
 instance was lost

Instances of launchers that live inside the control plane process do
not survive a restart, yet their Ready services kept pointing
status.endpoints at them and the gateway kept routing to dead
addresses.

mark_lost_instances(registry, launcher), meant to run at startup
before the controller, checks every Ready InferenceService: endpoints
whose instance the launcher does not run (or that carry no instance id
to check) become ready=false, the phase moves to Degraded and
Ready=False reports InstanceLost with a message telling the user to
delete and re-create the service. The gateway only routes to Ready
services, so it stops sending requests there once its cache expires.
Writes are compare-and-set on the version read; a service that changed
meanwhile is skipped. Nothing is relaunched: a Degraded service keeps
its allocation until it is deleted.
